Track 3: Maren and the Black Fairway
- Story & Context: Decades after the guild abandoned the harbor, coastal fishermen reported that the clockwork marimba left mounted in the rotting catwalk of Beacon Shoal Lighthouse had not wound down, driven perpetual by the rise and fall of weighted sea-floats in the surge pipe. Local pilots blamed the installation's endless, alien polyrhythms for luring the tugboat Aethelgard across the jagged granite bar during a dense October pea-souper, claiming the stone keys rang out intervals that no compass could navigate. When the wreckage drifted ashore, its hull was scored by meteor-iron mallets, while the lone radio beacon replayed the track's ghostly spoken refrain: "The rocks remember what the sky forgot."
